/* High / Medium guidance script · p-space (Discuss both views) · B1 tier, Band 4.0–5.0
   Built on the B2 Universal template starter lines (template.js b2-u-i, b2-u-a, b2-u-b, b2-u-c; B1 writers use the
   B2 template, T.Chris, 15 Nov 2026), populated with the prompt's B1 variables (prompts-levels.js vars.B1). Variable
   steps (v: …) use the same right answer as the Duelling Hall at B1; where the plan has already chosen a variable's
   meaning, the essay step tests its form instead. Modelled on the tested B2 script guide/p-space.js (same sections
   and step ids). Questions, options and hints rewritten for B1 readers; "weak point" names the nuance.
   One exception, reported to the lead: the B1 nuanceA ("…, so cutting them would change little") already contains
   "so", which doubles with the template's ", so this point has its limits". Step a-nu therefore writes the clause with
   "and" ("these budgets are … , and cutting them would change little") and uses its own near-misses, not the duel's,
   so that the duel and High never disagree.
   Examples are kept generic (a taxi driver, a team at a hospital): no named mission, figure or date.
   Standard: docs/GUIDE-AUTHORING-T2.md §12. Test: node tools/guide-test.js p-space.b1 --essay */
